---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import ReproductionLabel from '../../components/ReproductionLabel.astro';
import { methods, methodUrl, assetUrl } from '../../lib/evidence';
import { methodPresentation, sourceCapabilities } from '../../content/methods';
const support = [
  ['methods/__init__.py', 'Package initializer'],
  ['methods/demo.py', 'Synthetic demonstration runner'],
  ['tests/test_methods.py', 'Synthetic contract tests'],
  ['methods/ATTRIBUTION.json', 'Attribution and conceptual-source identities'],
  ['methods/validation.json', 'Archived example verification'],
  ['docs/METHODS.md', 'Full reviewed method documentation'],
  ['NOTICE.md', 'Reviewed material notice'],
];
---
<SiteLayout title="Methods" description="Five independently authored Python examples explain bounded mathematical and timing contracts, with synthetic output, assumptions, attribution and source downloads." type="method-index" reproduction="executable_example">
  <header class="page-heading"><span class="eyebrow">The reusable work / Five bounded examples</span><h1>Small methods.<br />Visible assumptions.</h1><p class="lede">Inspect the arithmetic and software behavior behind a research question. Each example has a narrow contract, a visible limitation and a verified synthetic output.</p><div class="evidence-note"><p><strong>Synthetic teaching example — not market evidence.</strong></p><p>These independent demonstrations do not replicate historical strategy returns, produce trading signals or establish a certified strategy.</p></div><ReproductionLabel level="executable_example"/></header>
  <ol class="record-list">
    {methods.map((method,index)=><li class="record-item"><div><span class="eyebrow">Example {String(index+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span><h2><a href={methodUrl(method.id)}>{method.title}</a></h2><p>{methodPresentation(method.id).summary}</p><a class="text-link" href={methodUrl(method.id)}>Read the example</a><p><a href={`/research/cases/${methodPresentation(method.id).relatedCase}/`}>Read the related investigation and recorded evidence</a></p></div><div class="record-meta"><span>Python standard library only</span><span>Independently authored</span><span>Reserved rights</span></div></li>)}
  </ol>
  <section id="run" class="section prose" aria-labelledby="run-title"><span class="eyebrow">Reproduction boundary</span><h2 id="run-title">Run the synthetic collection.</h2><p>The downloadable Python examples execute independently. The <a href="/research/walkthrough/">Momentum browser walkthrough</a>, <a href="/research/cases/price-bridge/#bridge-instrument">Bridge mechanism</a> and <a href="/engineering/">Inside Ardor stations</a> are separately authored browser explanations. They do not run the original research engines.</p><p>The five examples use Python’s standard library. Download the original files below, keeping the <code>methods/</code> and <code>tests/</code> paths under one folder. Run these commands from that folder. Python 3.12 is the supported handoff verification baseline.</p><pre tabindex="0" aria-label="Commands to run the included synthetic examples"><code>python3.12 -B -E -m unittest discover -s tests -p test_methods.py -v
python3.12 -B -E -m methods.demo</code></pre><p>The recorded output is generated from these unchanged examples and checked against the archived demonstration hash during the local build. The tests establish software contracts. They do not execute the historical research engines or resolve private data and source-rights limitations.</p><h3>Original example source</h3><ul>{methods.map(method=><li><a href={assetUrl(method.path)} download>{method.path}</a> — {method.title}</li>)}</ul><h3>Required support and notices</h3><ul>{support.map(([path,label])=><li><a href={assetUrl(path!)} download>{path}</a> — {label}</li>)}</ul><p class="small">Each download is an explicitly reviewed original file. This publication offers individual files; reuse remains subject to the applicable reserved-rights notices.</p></section>
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="capabilities-title"><span class="eyebrow">Source project context</span><h2 id="capabilities-title">Capability is a separate question.</h2><p style="max-width:75ch">The broader source inventory distinguishes implemented tools from specifications, scaffolds and unfinished work. Source presence and declared optional dependencies do not establish installation, execution, historical parity or trading capability. Historical source execution has not been verified for these examples.</p><div class="table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Source capability inventory" tabindex="0"><table><caption>Source capabilities and reproduction limits</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Capability</th><th scope="col">Source maturity</th><th scope="col">Reproduction limits</th></tr></thead><tbody>{sourceCapabilities.map(capability=><tr><th scope="row">{capability.title}</th><td>{capability.maturity.replaceAll('_',' ')}</td><td>{capability.treatment}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div><p class="small">Implemented ledger-integrity helpers do not resolve the historical seal discrepancies recorded in the evidence policy. <a href="/evidence/">Read the reproduction definitions and limitations.</a></p></section>
</SiteLayout>
